    INSERT INTO mcqs (topic_id, question, options, correct_index, explanation) VALUES
    (v_topic_id, 'A 76-year-old female named Beatrice is admitted to the hospital with multiple bruises, severe malnutrition, and cognitive decline. The medical team suspects elder abuse and neglect. Which of the following best describes the role of a multidisciplinary team in managing this patient''s care?', '["Transfer all decision-making authority to the hospital security team to handle the caregiver''s visits", "Rely solely on the primary care physician to investigate the home environment, find new housing, and file legal charges", "Discharge the patient as soon as the bruises fade, leaving the investigation entirely to the patient''s neighbors", "Coordinate care involving the geriatrician, social worker, Adult Protective Services (APS) caseworker, psychiatrist, and legal counsel to ensure the patient''s physical health, cognitive status, safety, and legal rights are addressed simultaneously", "Exclude the social worker and psychiatrist to prevent breaching the patient''s confidentiality during the investigation"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Managing elder abuse requires a **multidisciplinary team approach** because of the complex medical, psychological, social, and legal issues involved. The team typically includes: (1) **Geriatricians/Physicians** to diagnose and treat injuries and assess capacity, (2) **Social Workers** to coordinate resources and discharge planning, (3) **APS Caseworkers** to investigate safety and provide protective services, (4) **Psychiatrists** to evaluate cognitive and psychiatric conditions, and (5) **Legal Counsel** or elder law advocates to address guardianship and financial protection. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 14; Current Diagnosis & Treatment: Geriatrics Ch. 12)'),
